Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:21:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tests: build the widget tests against Qt 6.12

Qt 6.12 removed QTEST_DISABLE_KEYPAD_NAVIGATION from QtTest, so
W_QTEST_MAIN no longer compiles there, and with it every widget test
program, the extension tests the gate runs among them. Engine 6.11.2 is
built against Qt 6.12, as Arch builds its own qt6-webengine 6.11.2
(omaweb#660).

The macro did nothing, which is why qtbase removed it. This is Qt's
own change to the same line, backported unchanged. It drops when the
series moves to an engine that carries it.

qtwebengine c9300848e28ef0d8e9dfcfb29c5e1b2c5d43042f:
Fixes: QTBUG-147006
Change-Id: I4675020e79d85b7598967002863f44eb3a228e75

omaweb#660

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/auto/util/widgetutil.h | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/auto/util/widgetutil.h b/tests/auto/util/widgetutil.h
index 356d3c826c..3a3e0abbbf 100644
--- a/tests/auto/util/widgetutil.h
+++ b/tests/auto/util/widgetutil.h
@@ -24,7 +24,6 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) \
     \
     QApplication app(w_argc, const_cast<char **>(w_argv.data())); \
     app.setAttribute(Qt::AA_Use96Dpi, true); \
-    QTEST_DISABLE_KEYPAD_NAVIGATION \
     TestObject tc; \
     QTEST_SET_MAIN_SOURCE_PATH \
     return QTest::qExec(&tc, argc, argv); \
